S <NONO@NONE.com> writes:
> How does pets attacking peacefuls work? What relative level does the pet 
> need to be before it will attack on its own?

A pet will not attack a monster if:

* its level is two or more higher than the pet's
* it is a visible unblinded floating eye and the pet has eyes (90%)
* it is a gelatinous cube (90%)
* its passive-damage-dealing capacity is greater than the pet's HP
* it is peaceful and the pet is at less than 1/4 max HP and unconflicted
* it is a Quest Leader or guardian and the pet is unconflicted
* it is a *trice and the pet isn't stoning resistant

> I so need a robe, and Grrl is XL 8, ~61 HP, fast. The Minetown priest is 
